    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The exact order of planets from the Sun is Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, and Neptune.",
        "Mercury, Venus, Earth, and Mars are categorized as inner/terrestrial planets.",
        "Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, and Neptune constitute the outer planets (gas and ice giants)."
      ],
      "id": "3oui6nb"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Competitive exams frequently test the correct sequence of planets from nearest to farthest from the Sun.",
        "Use popular mnemonics such as 'My Very Educated Mother Just Served Us Noodles' for quick recall during exams."
